      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "buildJavaScript": "You are helping a beginner student learning arrays in JavaScript.\n\nWrite simple JavaScript code that displays items from an existing array called favoritesArray.\n\nUse index positions 0, 1, and 2. Do not use loops, functions, or advanced syntax.\n\nUse document.getElementById(\"item0\"), \"item1\", and \"item2\" to display the values.\n\nDo not modify or recreate the array. Do not rename variables.\n\nReturn only valid JavaScript code. No explanation, no extra text.\n\nExample:\n\ndocument.getElementById(\"item0\").textContent = favoritesArray[0];\ndocument.getElementById(\"item1\").textContent = favoritesArray[1];\ndocument.getElementById(\"item2\").textContent = favoritesArray[2];"
